---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy — After High School" description="What afterhighschool.me collects, why, and what we never do with it." path="/privacy">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>Most people using this site are in high school, so we collect as little as we can and say exactly what happens to it.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>If you join the waitlist: your email address, whether you're a student, parent, counselor or something else, and the date you signed up. That's all.</p>

      <h2>What we use it for</h2>
      <p>To email you when the site's tools open, and occasionally with updates about the project. Every email has a way to unsubscribe.</p>

      <h2>What we never do</h2>
      <p>We don't sell or rent your information. We don't share it with colleges, advertisers or data brokers. We don't use advertising trackers.</p>

      <h2>Kids under 13</h2>
      <p>The waitlist is for people 13 and older. If you think a child under 13 has signed up, email us and we'll delete it.</p>

      <h2>Deleting your information</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@afterhighschool.me">hello@afterhighschool.me</a> from the address you signed up with and we'll remove it.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>We count page visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which doesn't use cookies or track you across sites.</p>

      <h2>Your grades, scores and saved schools</h2>
      <p>When you enter your GPA or test scores in "Where you'd stand", or save schools to My list, they're kept in your own browser (its local storage) so they fill in on other pages. They never leave your device and we never see them. Clearing your browser's site data for afterhighschool.me removes them.</p>

      <p><em>Last updated November 5, 2026.</em></p>
    </article>
  <p slot="footer"><a href="/">Back to afterhighschool.me</a></p>
</Layout>
